// Curated ingredient catalog: the single list of ingredients the app can
// calculate nutrition for.
//
// Every entry is tied to a published nutrition record:
//   fdc:   USDA FoodData Central, SR Legacy dataset (April 2018 release). The
//          nutrient values and household-measure weights are NOT typed here;
//          scripts/buildIngredientDb.mjs reads them from the USDA CSV files
//          and writes data/ingredientDb.json.
//   label: a USDA FoodData Central *Branded Foods* record (a real product
//          label) for ingredients SR Legacy does not cover (paneer, Thai curry
//          pastes, light coconut milk ...). Values are copied from that record
//          per 100 g (or 100 ml), with the brand, so they can be re-checked.
//
// Fields
//   id        stable ingredient ID used across recipes, steps and the database
//   name      standard ingredient name
//   aliases   other names the ingredient is written as (matched as whole words)
//   cat       ingredient category
//   state     raw | cooked | dry | canned | prepared (state the values refer to)
//   animal    animal origin, for diet checks: meat | poultry | fish | shellfish | dairy | egg | honey
//   allergens major allergens it contains
//   mayContain allergens/animal products that depend on the brand (e.g. curry
//             pastes made with shrimp paste) — the recipe must name a safe product
//   gluten    true when it contains gluten; 'cross-contact' for oats
//   portions  household-measure weights (g) used only where USDA has none,
//             each with the reason in portionNote
//   variability brand-to-brand spread worth telling the cook about
//   negligible quantities used are too small to matter nutritionally (whole leaves)

const LABEL = (fdcId, brand, per100g, note) => ({ fdcId, brand, per100g, note });

